nifmake builds with nimony (and still with classic Nim), so the self-hosted lane can run it on Temen.

Why: nimony's build driver (`nimony c` / `check`) hands the dependency graph to nifmake, and the
self-hosted lane (#1609) runs every phase as a Temen module compiled by nimony with no C. Upstream
nifmake is a classic-Nim-only program: it uses stdlib conveniences nimony's stdlib does not have
(`setLastModificationTime`, `tables.withValue`, `align`/`alignLeft`, `os.sleep`, multi-argument
`writeLine`, `except ValueError`, a capturing `sort` comparator, a nil `ptr`, raising table and OS
calls outside `try`). It also fixes a latent bug:
`countProcessors()` is 0 when the count cannot be detected, and `-j` then scheduled nothing and
reported the unbuilt graph as a success. Not fixed upstream as of nim-lang/nimony master b2c2df77 (2026-09-23).

What: every change is either `when defined(nimony)` or shared code valid under both compilers,
using upstream's own dual-compile idioms (`lib/compat2.nim`'s `onRaiseQuit` / `getOrQuit`).
Behaviour is unchanged: the patched file builds with classic Nim 2.2.10 and with nimony, and
either binary drives `nimony c` to the same result.

Applied to a COPY of the pinned sources at build time (`scripts/ci/nim-selfhost-lane.sh`); the
vendored `nimony/` submodule is never modified. Against the submodule pin (v0.6.2, 851fe262).
Drop it when upstream nifmake builds with nimony.
